## C. Collapse the three text-size ladders into data plus one renderer

The file currently defines:

```latex
\BookModeTextSizes
\MobileModeTextSizes
\AlphabetHistoryMobileTextSizes
```

each containing repeated calls to:

```latex
\DeclareConfiguredTextSize
```

with different values.

This is good data represented inefficiently as executable declarations.

Represent the ladders as data:

```lua
book.text_size_profiles = {
    book = {
        tiny        = {"6pt", "7pt"},
        scriptsize  = {"8pt", "9.5pt"},
        footnotesize= {"9pt", "11pt"},
        ...
    },

    mobile = {
        tiny        = {"8pt", "9.33pt"},
        ...
    },

    alphabet_mobile = {
        tiny        = {"7.5pt", "8.75pt"},
        ...
    },
}
```

Then write **one** TeX/Lua mechanism that applies a named size profile.

This is a representative refactoring principle for the entire file:

> If twenty lines have exactly the same structure and differ only in values, the structure is code and the values are data.

Keep them separate.

