## D. Keep font declarations in TeX, but move the font catalog metadata into one coherent registry

The enormous historical-font section contains dozens of individually named font families:

```latex
\ProtoSinaiticFifteenthCenturyFont
\ProtoSinaiticThirteenthCenturyFont
\ProtoSinaiticIzbetSartahFont
\PaleoHebrewTelZayitFont
\PaleoHebrewGezerFont
\PaleoHebrewTelDanFont
\PaleoHebrewMoabiteFont
\PaleoHebrewSiloamFont
\PaleoHebrewKetefHinnomAFont
\PaleoHebrewKetefHinnomBFont
\PaleoHebrewLachishAFont
...
```

Actual `fontspec` font declarations need to exist on the TeX side, so do not contort Lua into defining fonts if doing so makes the boundary worse.

But separate:

```text
FONT EXISTENCE
```

from:

```text
FONT METADATA AND ROLE
```

A central Lua catalog can describe the latter:

```lua
book.fonts = {
    paleo_tel_zayit = {
        tex = "PaleoHebrewTelZayitFont",
        script = "historical_hebrew_ascii",
        period = "...",
        default_scale = 1.71,
