## F. Delete most of the encoder-specific TeX wrapper macros

The existing implementation exposes a long chain like:

```latex
\HebrewNoNiqqud
\HebrewRaw
\HebrewToPaleoASCII
\HebrewForPaleoUnicode
\HebrewToPaleoHebrewPhoenician
\HebrewToAramaic

\EncodeHebrewNoNiqqud
\EncodeHebrewRaw
\EncodePaleoASCII
\EncodePaleoUnicode
\EncodeProtoA
\EncodeProtoB
\EncodeProtoC
...
\EncodePaleoA
\EncodePaleoB
...
```

Most of these differ only by an encoder name.

Internally, replace them with one generic operation, conceptually:

```latex
\EncodeHebrew{proto_a}{...}
```

which calls:

```lua
paleotex.encode(text, "proto_a")
```

Then retain old names **only where useful as compatibility wrappers**:

```latex
\newcommand{\EncodeProtoA}[1]{\EncodeHebrew{proto_a}{#1}}
```

If no chapter/content file directly uses a compatibility name, remove it entirely.

Do not preserve an internal API merely because `master.tex` happens to have one.

