## H. Source categories, traits, authors, and render profiles need to become one coherent model

This is probably the single most important refactor in the file.

At present, source semantics are spread across several different mechanisms.

There are broad stylistic traits:

```latex
\PriestStyle
\LeviteStyle
\Native
\MushiteStyle
\AaronidStyle
\Yahwist
\Record
\Poetry
\OtherSource
```

There is a generic `\SourceDecorate` command containing a large string-dispatch table:

```latex
plain
regular
native
priest
bold
nopriest
nobold
levite
mushite
aaronid
yahwist
dtr1
dtr2
dtn
jeremiah
ezekiel
record
records
other
poetry
italic
noitalic
mono
law
redactor
bg
...
```

Then there are `\DeclareSourceProfile` calls that separately bind:

```text
English font
English style
Hebrew renderer
Hebrew style
```

for sources such as:

```text
J
E
DtrA
DtrB
DtrH
Dtn
P
PP
R
X
Aramaic
RJE
Records
Other
Proto*
Paleo*
```

This is already revealing the correct conceptual structure.

Make it explicit.

A source record might conceptually resemble:

```lua
book.sources = {
    J = {
        category = "native",
        group = nil,

        english = {
            font = "english",
            color = "Jcolor",
            weight = "medium",
        },

        hebrew = {
            renderer = "phoenician",
            color = "Jcolor",
            weight = "medium",
        },

        background = "Jbgcolor",
    },

    E = {
        category = "priest",
        group = "mushite",

        english = {
            font = "english",
            scale = 0.96,
