## O. Avoid duplicating style names and color names where one semantic token suffices

For example, the file includes aliases such as:

```latex
\colorlet{RecordsColor}{Recordcolor}
```

and:

```latex
\let\DeuteronomistAStyle\DeuterAStyle
\let\DeuteronomistBStyle\DeuterBStyle
\let\DeuteronomicLawStyle\DeuterNStyle
```

Some aliases exist for good compatibility reasons.

Others may merely be accumulated naming history.

Inspect actual usage.

Where two names are public and heavily used, preserve the alias cheaply.

Where one is dead or internal, remove it.

Do not maintain multiple conceptual names for the same object unless they provide real value.

