## AY. Refactoring test: ask whether changing one fact requires touching one place

Use this as a continuous architecture test.

If I want to:

```text
change E's Hebrew font
```

I should change one source-profile field.

If I want to:

```text
change P from Aaronid blue to another semantic style
```

I should change one profile/category definition.

If I want to:

```text
change Genesis chapter 16's summary
```

I should change one summary string.

If I want to:

```text
add a new source
```

I should add one source record, and its normal public renderer commands should appear automatically.

If I want to:

```text
switch mobile geometry
```

I should edit the mobile output profile.

If I want to:

```text
change the default commentary author's foreground
```

I should edit commentary profile A.

If I want to:

```text
add a new book with 12 normal sequential chapter files
```

I should not have to write 12 `\include` lines manually.

If any of these operations still require updating several synchronized macro registries, continue refactoring.

